01:03:37.250 --> 01:03:39.583
this morning on the list.

01:03:39.583 --> 01:03:42.167
It's-- Oh, I know this.

01:03:39.583 --> 01:03:42.167
It's something to do with--

01:03:42.167 --> 01:03:47.667
Wait, he was--

01:03:42.167 --> 01:03:47.667
he was part of the--

01:03:42.167 --> 01:03:47.667
Oh, God, I know this. Um--

01:03:47.667 --> 01:03:52.750
It's Ambassador Franklin,

01:03:47.667 --> 01:03:52.750
and that's the woman that

01:03:47.667 --> 01:03:52.750
he left his wife for, Rebecca.

01:03:54.792 --> 01:03:57.708
-Rebecca. Ambassador.

01:03:54.792 --> 01:03:57.708
-Miranda.

01:03:57.708 --> 01:04:00.625
-You look fabulous.

01:03:57.708 --> 01:04:00.625
-Oh, very kind.

01:04:00.625 --> 01:04:03.917
-Thank you.

01:04:00.625 --> 01:04:03.917
-(chattering continues)

01:04:11.625 --> 01:04:13.875
-Look at you.

01:04:11.625 --> 01:04:13.875
-Hello.

01:04:13.875 --> 01:04:15.833
You're--

01:04:13.875 --> 01:04:15.833
You're a vision.

01:04:15.833 --> 01:04:18.833
-Oh. (scoffs)

01:04:15.833 --> 01:04:18.833
-Thank God I saved your job.

01:04:18.833 --> 01:04:23.750
(stammers, chuckles)

01:04:18.833 --> 01:04:23.750
You know, I figured out

01:04:18.833 --> 01:04:23.750
a few things on my own too.

01:04:23.750 --> 01:04:26.333
Turns out, I'm not as nice

01:04:23.750 --> 01:04:26.333
as you thought.

01:04:26.333 --> 01:04:28.583
I hope not.

01:04:28.583 --> 01:04:30.875
Well, if it weren't

01:04:28.583 --> 01:04:30.875
for the stupid boyfriend,

01:04:30.875 --> 01:04:33.333
I'd have to whisk you away

01:04:30.875 --> 01:04:33.333
right here and now.

01:04:35.375 --> 01:04:39.500
-Do you actually say things

01:04:35.375 --> 01:04:39.500
like that to people?

01:04:35.375 --> 01:04:39.500
-Evidently.

01:04:39.500 --> 01:04:42.250
(giggles)

01:04:39.500 --> 01:04:42.250
Well, I gotta go.

01:04:42.250 --> 01:04:45.208
Are you sure? 'Cause my editor

01:04:42.250 --> 01:04:45.208
for<i> New York Magazine </i>is inside,

01:04:45.208 --> 01:04:48.417
and, you know,

01:04:45.208 --> 01:04:48.417
I could introduce you two.

01:04:48.417 --> 01:04:52.083
-You sent over your stuff

01:04:48.417 --> 01:04:52.083
for me to look at? Remember?

01:04:48.417 --> 01:04:52.083
-Yeah.

01:04:52.083 --> 01:04:56.333
All right, I gotta admit,

01:04:52.083 --> 01:04:56.333
I only read a couple. It was

01:04:52.083 --> 01:04:56.333
a very large packet you sent.

01:04:56.333 --> 01:04:58.917
-Yeah.

01:04:56.333 --> 01:04:58.917
-But what I did read

01:04:56.333 --> 01:04:58.917
wasn't half bad.

01:04:58.917 --> 01:05:01.583
And, you know, I think--

01:04:58.917 --> 01:05:01.583
I think you have a talent, Andy.

01:05:01.583 --> 01:05:04.458
He should meet you.

01:05:04.458 --> 01:05:06.375
Why don't you come in?

01:05:04.458 --> 01:05:06.375
Just for one drink.

01:05:06.375 --> 01:05:10.333
Um, okay, yeah.

01:05:06.375 --> 01:05:10.333
I guess I could for one--

01:05:10.333 --> 01:05:14.125
No, I can't.

01:05:10.333 --> 01:05:14.125
I'm sorry,

01:05:10.333 --> 01:05:14.125
but I have to go.

01:05:14.125 --> 01:05:17.042
All right. Give my best

01:05:14.125 --> 01:05:17.042
to the boyfriend.

01:05:24.792 --> 01:05:27.250
Roy, I'm sorry.

01:05:24.792 --> 01:05:27.250
Can you go any faster?

01:05:27.250 --> 01:05:29.542
I'm sure Nate will understand.

01:05:32.375 --> 01:05:34.250
Yeah.

01:05:34.250 --> 01:05:37.083
(TV, indistinct)

01:05:37.083 --> 01:05:39.250
Hey.

01:05:54.125 --> 01:05:56.292
Happy birthday.

01:06:00.375 --> 01:06:03.250
Nate, I'm so sorry.

01:06:03.250 --> 01:06:07.542
I kept trying to leave,

01:06:03.250 --> 01:06:07.542
but there was a lot going on.

01:06:07.542 --> 01:06:09.667
And, you know,

01:06:07.542 --> 01:06:09.667
I didn't have a choice.

01:06:09.667 --> 01:06:11.583
Don't worry about it.

01:06:11.583 --> 01:06:14.500
(grunts)

01:06:11.583 --> 01:06:14.500
I'm gonna go to bed.

01:06:16.625 --> 01:06:18.458
Can we at least

01:06:16.625 --> 01:06:18.458
talk about this?

01:06:27.167 --> 01:06:28.875
You look really pretty.

01:07:10.917 --> 01:07:12.417
MIRANDA:

01:07:10.917 --> 01:07:12.417
Andrea?

01:07:24.917 --> 01:07:28.625
-Do you have the Book?

01:07:24.917 --> 01:07:28.625
-Oh. Uh--

01:07:30.708 --> 01:07:32.083
Mm.

01:07:33.625 --> 01:07:37.000
Paris is

01:07:33.625 --> 01:07:37.000
the most important week

01:07:33.625 --> 01:07:37.000
of my entire year.

01:07:37.000 --> 01:07:39.708
I need the best

01:07:37.000 --> 01:07:39.708
possible team with me.

01:07:41.708 --> 01:07:44.250
That no longer

01:07:41.708 --> 01:07:44.250
includes Emily.

01:07:46.292 --> 01:07:48.208
Wait.

01:07:46.292 --> 01:07:48.208
You want me to--

01:07:49.208 --> 01:07:52.708
(stammering) No, Miranda.

01:07:52.708 --> 01:07:55.167
(exhales)

01:07:52.708 --> 01:07:55.167
Emily would die.

01:07:55.167 --> 01:07:57.958
Her whole life

01:07:55.167 --> 01:07:57.958
is about Paris.

01:07:57.958 --> 01:08:02.917
She hasn't eaten in weeks.

01:07:57.958 --> 01:08:02.917
I-I can't... do that.

01:08:02.917 --> 01:08:05.417
Miranda, I can't.

01:08:05.417 --> 01:08:07.250
If you don't go,

01:08:05.417 --> 01:08:07.250
I'll assume you're not serious

01:08:07.250 --> 01:08:11.042
about your future

01:08:07.250 --> 01:08:11.042
at<i> Runway </i>or...

01:08:11.042 --> 01:08:13.083
any other publication.

01:08:18.583 --> 01:08:20.833
The decision's yours.

01:08:22.833 --> 01:08:24.333
That's all.

01:08:32.500 --> 01:08:35.833
(down-tempo music playing)

01:08:35.833 --> 01:08:40.542
<i>♪ Fill these spaces</i>

01:08:35.833 --> 01:08:40.542
<i>up with days ♪</i>

01:08:42.917 --> 01:08:45.417
<i>♪ In my room ♪</i>

01:08:45.417 --> 01:08:49.292
<i>♪ You can go</i>

01:08:45.417 --> 01:08:49.292
<i>you can stay ♪</i>

01:08:49.292 --> 01:08:51.625
(laughing)

01:08:51.625 --> 01:08:55.083
<i>♪ I can't sleep ♪</i>

01:08:56.083 --> 01:09:00.833
<i>♪ I can't speak to you ♪</i>

01:09:00.833 --> 01:09:04.417
<i>♪ I can't sleep ♪</i>

01:09:12.708 --> 01:09:17.125
<i>♪ Now these years</i>

01:09:12.708 --> 01:09:17.125
<i>locked in my drawer ♪</i>

01:09:19.500 --> 01:09:22.125
<i>♪ I'll open to see ♪</i>

01:09:23.833 --> 01:09:27.500
<i>-♪ Just to be sure ♪</i>

01:09:23.833 --> 01:09:27.500
-Hey, Andy.

01:09:27.500 --> 01:09:30.125
-Hey.

01:09:27.500 --> 01:09:30.125
-You coming to bed

01:09:27.500 --> 01:09:30.125
anytime soon?

01:09:30.125 --> 01:09:33.417
Uh, yeah.

01:09:30.125 --> 01:09:33.417
Five minutes, okay?

01:09:33.417 --> 01:09:37.792
<i>♪ I can't speak to you ♪</i>

01:09:37.792 --> 01:09:41.583
<i>♪ I can't sleep ♪</i>

01:09:42.792 --> 01:09:44.708
(sighs)

01:09:54.917 --> 01:09:57.542
(fax printing)

01:10:07.250 --> 01:10:08.875
(clears throat)

01:10:28.375 --> 01:10:31.000
Andrea, don't forget

01:10:28.375 --> 01:10:31.000
to tell Emily.

01:10:32.958 --> 01:10:34.583
Do it now.

01:10:44.208 --> 01:10:47.125
-(line ringing)

01:10:44.208 --> 01:10:47.125
-Don't pick up.

01:10:47.125 --> 01:10:49.792
-Don't pick up.

01:10:47.125 --> 01:10:49.792
Don't pick up. Don't pick--

01:10:47.125 --> 01:10:49.792
<i>-Hi.</i>

01:10:49.792 --> 01:10:51.917
-Emily.

01:10:49.792 --> 01:10:51.917
<i>-Hi, hi. Sorry I'm late.</i>

01:10:51.917 --> 01:10:54.833
It's just Miranda wanted

01:10:51.917 --> 01:10:54.833
some scarves from Hermès.

01:10:54.833 --> 01:10:57.417
And she did tell me yesterday,

01:10:54.833 --> 01:10:57.417
but I forgot like an idiot.

01:10:57.417 --> 01:10:59.458
<i>And so I freaked out,</i>

01:10:57.417 --> 01:10:59.458
<i>of course.</i>

01:10:59.458 --> 01:11:02.250
Emily, Emily,

01:10:59.458 --> 01:11:02.250
I-I need to talk to you.

01:11:02.250 --> 01:11:05.083
I called Martine at home,

01:11:02.250 --> 01:11:05.083
and she opened the shop early.

01:11:02.250 --> 01:11:05.083
Whoa! I'm sorry.

01:11:05.083 --> 01:11:08.292
She opened the shop early

01:11:05.083 --> 01:11:08.292
for me, so I got them,

01:11:05.083 --> 01:11:08.292
which is great.

01:11:08.292 --> 01:11:11.708
Okay. Um, Emily,

01:11:08.292 --> 01:11:11.708
wh-when you come in,

01:11:11.708 --> 01:11:13.875
there's something

01:11:11.708 --> 01:11:13.875
I have to talk to you about.

01:11:13.875 --> 01:11:17.083
<i>-Well, I hope it's not</i>

01:11:13.875 --> 01:11:17.083
<i>another Miranda problem.</i>

01:11:13.875 --> 01:11:17.083
-Not exactly.

01:11:17.083 --> 01:11:20.792
Well, good, because

01:11:17.083 --> 01:11:20.792
I've got so much to deal with

01:11:17.083 --> 01:11:20.792
before I go. I swear to God--

01:11:20.792 --> 01:11:23.333
-(gasps)

01:11:20.792 --> 01:11:23.333
-(horn honks)

01:11:23.333 --> 01:11:27.792
-(people exclaiming)

01:11:23.333 --> 01:11:27.792
-WOMAN: Oh, my God!

01:11:27.792 --> 01:11:29.667
Emily?

01:11:29.667 --> 01:11:32.500
(woman on P.A., indistinct)

01:11:32.500 --> 01:11:34.500
(elevator bell dings)

01:11:38.417 --> 01:11:42.917
I don't care if she was

01:11:38.417 --> 01:11:42.917
gonna fire you or beat you

01:11:38.417 --> 01:11:42.917
with a red-hot poker!

01:11:42.917 --> 01:11:44.583
You should have said no.

01:11:44.583 --> 01:11:46.583
Emily, I didn't have a choice.

01:11:46.583 --> 01:11:48.583
-Oh. Please.

01:11:46.583 --> 01:11:48.583
-You know how she is.

01:11:48.583 --> 01:11:51.417
-That is a pathetic excuse.

01:11:48.583 --> 01:11:51.417
-(door opens)

01:11:55.083 --> 01:11:57.208
Thanks.

01:11:57.208 --> 01:11:59.583
Do you know

01:11:57.208 --> 01:11:59.583
what really just...

01:11:59.583 --> 01:12:02.583
gets me about

01:11:59.583 --> 01:12:02.583
this whole thing,

01:12:02.583 --> 01:12:06.708
is that, you know, you're

01:12:02.583 --> 01:12:06.708
the one who said you don't

01:12:02.583 --> 01:12:06.708
really care about this stuff.

01:12:06.708 --> 01:12:10.958
And you don't really care

01:12:06.708 --> 01:12:10.958
about fashion. You just

01:12:06.708 --> 01:12:10.958
wanna be a journalist.

01:12:10.958 --> 01:12:12.875
What a pile of bollocks!

01:12:12.875 --> 01:12:15.333
Emily, I know you're mad.

01:12:12.875 --> 01:12:15.333
I don't blame you.

01:12:15.333 --> 01:12:19.083
Face it, you sold your soul

01:12:15.333 --> 01:12:19.083
the day you put on that first

01:12:15.333 --> 01:12:19.083
pair of Jimmy Choo's.

01:12:19.083 --> 01:12:24.208
I saw it. And you know

01:12:19.083 --> 01:12:24.208
what really just kills me

01:12:19.083 --> 01:12:24.208
about this whole thing,

01:12:24.208 --> 01:12:26.417
is the clothes

01:12:24.208 --> 01:12:26.417
that you're gonna get.

01:12:26.417 --> 01:12:29.083
I mean,

01:12:26.417 --> 01:12:29.083
you don't deserve them.

01:12:29.083 --> 01:12:32.208
You eat carbs,

01:12:29.083 --> 01:12:32.208
for Christ's sake.

01:12:32.208 --> 01:12:36.417
God, it's so unfair!

01:12:36.417 --> 01:12:38.833
-Emily.

01:12:36.417 --> 01:12:38.833
-Just go.

01:12:45.083 --> 01:12:47.458
-Emily, I--

01:12:45.083 --> 01:12:47.458
-I said go!

01:12:51.167 --> 01:12:53.208
(sighs)

01:12:53.208 --> 01:12:55.667
-DOUG: You are going to Paris

01:12:53.208 --> 01:12:55.667
for the couture shows?

01:12:53.208 --> 01:12:55.667
-ANDY: Mm-hmm.

01:12:55.667 --> 01:12:58.792
-That's the coolest

01:12:55.667 --> 01:12:58.792
fashion event of the year.

01:12:55.667 --> 01:12:58.792
-Mm-hmm.

01:12:58.792 --> 01:13:01.292
-I mean, who are you

01:12:58.792 --> 01:13:01.292
going to see, Galliano?

01:12:58.792 --> 01:13:01.292
-Yeah.

01:13:01.292 --> 01:13:03.833
-And Lagerfeld

01:13:01.292 --> 01:13:03.833
and Nicholas Ghesquiere.

01:13:01.292 --> 01:13:03.833
-Yep.

01:13:03.833 --> 01:13:06.708
-Yes. Okay,

01:13:03.833 --> 01:13:06.708
now you're scaring me.

01:13:03.833 --> 01:13:06.708
-(chuckles)

01:13:06.708 --> 01:13:10.042
-Hey.

01:13:06.708 --> 01:13:10.042
-Hey.

01:13:10.042 --> 01:13:14.042
-This show is amazing.

01:13:10.042 --> 01:13:14.042
I am so proud of you.

01:13:10.042 --> 01:13:14.042
-LILY: Thank you.

01:13:14.042 --> 01:13:17.042
Okay, start with

01:13:14.042 --> 01:13:17.042
the photos in the back

01:13:14.042 --> 01:13:17.042
and work your way forward.

01:13:17.042 --> 01:13:18.458
That is the way

01:13:17.042 --> 01:13:18.458
I designed it.

01:13:18.458 --> 01:13:19.667
It is brilliant.

01:13:18.458 --> 01:13:19.667
You will love it.

01:13:19.667 --> 01:13:21.458
-Of course.

01:13:19.667 --> 01:13:21.458
-And you,

01:13:21.458 --> 01:13:23.042
I have somebody

01:13:21.458 --> 01:13:23.042
I want you to meet, okay?

01:13:23.042 --> 01:13:25.458
-Ooh, art and sex.

01:13:23.042 --> 01:13:25.458
-Lead the way.

01:13:25.458 --> 01:13:27.417
-See you later.

01:13:25.458 --> 01:13:27.417
-Okay.

01:13:28.750 --> 01:13:31.125
(down-tempo music playing)

01:13:33.208 --> 01:13:36.458
<i>♪ I've no regrets ♪</i>

01:13:36.458 --> 01:13:40.667
<i>♪ Every single work I find ♪</i>

01:13:42.167 --> 01:13:45.500
<i>♪ Don't hold our breath ♪</i>

01:13:45.500 --> 01:13:50.083
<i>-♪ Wait for another sign ♪</i>

01:13:45.500 --> 01:13:50.083
-Hey. Hey, Miranda girl.

01:13:51.667 --> 01:13:55.750
-Hi.

01:13:51.667 --> 01:13:55.750
-I was just thinking

01:13:51.667 --> 01:13:55.750
about you.

01:13:55.750 --> 01:13:57.583
Oh, come on.

01:13:57.583 --> 01:13:59.292
-It's true.

01:13:57.583 --> 01:13:59.292
-No.

01:13:59.292 --> 01:14:02.333
I'm profiling Gaultier

01:13:59.292 --> 01:14:02.333
for<i> Interview</i>

01:14:02.333 --> 01:14:04.458
and, uh, making

01:14:02.333 --> 01:14:04.458
my Paris plans.

01:14:04.458 --> 01:14:08.750
I found myself wondering

01:14:04.458 --> 01:14:08.750
if, uh, you were gonna be there.

01:14:08.750 --> 01:14:14.167
Well, actually,

01:14:08.750 --> 01:14:14.167
um, I am going.

01:14:14.167 --> 01:14:18.958
Great. I'm staying

01:14:14.167 --> 01:14:18.958
in a fantastic little hotel

01:14:14.167 --> 01:14:18.958
in the Seventh,

01:14:18.958 --> 01:14:22.792
right across the street

01:14:18.958 --> 01:14:22.792
from the falafel restaurant

01:14:18.958 --> 01:14:22.792
that will change your life.

01:14:22.792 --> 01:14:27.875
(chuckles) I'm sorry.

01:14:22.792 --> 01:14:27.875
I'll be too busy working.

01:14:27.875 --> 01:14:31.083
You'll have to find

01:14:27.875 --> 01:14:31.083
someone else's life

01:14:27.875 --> 01:14:31.083
to change.

01:14:32.125 --> 01:14:34.458
Well, that's just it.

01:14:34.458 --> 01:14:36.708
I'm beginning to wonder

01:14:34.458 --> 01:14:36.708
if I can.

01:14:49.917 --> 01:14:52.875
Lily.

01:14:52.875 --> 01:14:55.208
Lily, he's just a guy

01:14:52.875 --> 01:14:55.208
I know from work.

01:14:55.208 --> 01:14:58.083
-Yeah, that looked like work.

01:14:55.208 --> 01:14:58.083
-Look, you're making

01:14:55.208 --> 01:14:58.083
a big deal out of--

01:14:58.083 --> 01:15:01.583
You know, the Andy I know

01:14:58.083 --> 01:15:01.583
is madly in love with Nate,

01:15:01.583 --> 01:15:03.875
is always

01:15:01.583 --> 01:15:03.875
five minutes early...

01:15:03.875 --> 01:15:06.667
and thinks, I don't know,

01:15:03.875 --> 01:15:06.667
Club Monaco is couture.

01:15:06.667 --> 01:15:10.333
For the last 16 years,

01:15:06.667 --> 01:15:10.333
I've known everything

01:15:06.667 --> 01:15:10.333
about that Andy.

01:15:10.333 --> 01:15:14.333
But this person?

01:15:10.333 --> 01:15:14.333
This "glamazon" who skulks

01:15:10.333 --> 01:15:14.333
around in corners...

01:15:14.333 --> 01:15:16.458
with some random

01:15:14.333 --> 01:15:16.458
hot fashion guy?

01:15:17.458 --> 01:15:18.708
I don't get her.

01:15:20.500 --> 01:15:23.125
-Lily.

01:15:20.500 --> 01:15:23.125
-Have fun in Paris.

01:15:24.500 --> 01:15:26.500
You going to Paris?

01:15:26.500 --> 01:15:29.583
Uh, yeah.

01:15:26.500 --> 01:15:29.583
It just happened.

01:15:29.583 --> 01:15:33.208
I thought Paris

01:15:29.583 --> 01:15:33.208
was a big deal

01:15:29.583 --> 01:15:33.208
for Emily or--

01:15:33.208 --> 01:15:35.542
Great. Now you're gonna

01:15:33.208 --> 01:15:35.542
give me a hard time too?

01:15:37.708 --> 01:15:41.458
Hey, Andy. Andy!

01:15:41.458 --> 01:15:44.625
-Andy, what the hell

01:15:41.458 --> 01:15:44.625
is wrong with you?

01:15:41.458 --> 01:15:44.625
-I-I didn't have a choice, okay?

01:15:44.625 --> 01:15:46.958
-Miranda asked me,

01:15:44.625 --> 01:15:46.958
and I couldn't say no.

01:15:44.625 --> 01:15:46.958
-I know.

